Purpose

Authentication se related saare API endpoints define karta hai, jaise registration, login, Google login, email verification, password reset aur profile APIs.

Endpoints
POST /auth/register

Purpose:
Naya user register karta hai aur email verification code generate/send karta hai.

Request:
name, email, password

Response:
Registration successful message aur email.

POST /auth/verify-email

Purpose:
Verification code ke through user ka email verify karta hai.

Request:
email, code

Response:
Verification successful hone par JWT token aur user details.

POST /auth/login

Purpose:
Email aur password se user ko authenticate karta hai.

Request:
email, password

Response:
Valid credentials hone par JWT token aur user details.

POST /auth/google

Purpose:
Google credential verify karke user ko login/register karta hai.

Request:
credential

Response:
JWT token aur user details.

POST /auth/forgot-password

Purpose:
Password reset ke liye reset token generate karke user ko reset link bhejta hai.

Request:
email

Response:
Password reset link sent message.

POST /auth/reset-password/:token

Purpose:
Valid reset token ke through user ka password change karta hai.

Request:
password

Response:
Password reset successful message.

PUT /auth/update-name

Purpose:
Logged-in user ka name update karta hai.

Authentication:
protect middleware required.

Request:
name

Response:
Updated name.

GET /auth/profile

Purpose:
Logged-in user ki profile information retrieve karta hai.

Authentication:
protect middleware required.

Response:
User ID, name, email, profile photo aur verification status.

POST /auth/resend-code

Purpose:
Unverified user ke liye naya email verification code generate aur send karta hai.

Request:
email

Response:
New verification code sent message.

Authentication Flow
Register
   ↓
Verify Email
   ↓
JWT Token
   ↓
Login / Protected APIs